# Project Rules for KeepEat (Cursor IDE)

> Automatically loaded by Cursor IDE when opening this project
> Source of truth: `.ai/core-rules.md`

## Rule Priority (in case of conflict)

1. `.ai/core-rules.md` — universal, non-negotiable rules
2. `.ai/task-flow.md` — development workflow
3. `.ai/test-policy.md` — testing architecture
4. `.ai/review-checklist.md` — self-review template
5. `.ai/stacks/<stack>.md` — stack-specific conventions

Load these files and follow strictly.

## Critical Rules (Summary)

### Testing Mandate
- **Bug fix** → Regression test (mandatory, must fail first)
- **Feature** → Acceptance test (mandatory)
- Never suppress or weaken existing tests
- Never mock business logic (only I/O, external services)

### Development Discipline
- Inspect existing code first, then modify
- Reuse hooks, utilities, components (three+ lines → extract)
- Follow KeepEat product rules:
  - No fake-personalized UI
  - No scattered `console.log`
  - No parallel data flows for same product
  - Debug tools via config only
  - Never suppress errors silently

### Validation & Commits
- **Before every commit**: `./scripts/ai-validate.sh --quick`
- **Before every push**: `./scripts/ai-validate.sh` (full)
- Pre-commit hook enforces: `verify-tests-added.mjs`
- Pre-push hook enforces: full `ai-validate.sh`

### Git Discipline
- ❌ `git push --force`
- ❌ `git commit --no-verify`
- ✅ Feature branch → PR → merge
- Commit format: `<type>(<scope>): <description>`

### Code Quality
- **Frontend**: TypeScript strict, no `any`
- **Backend**: mypy strict, no `type: ignore`
- **Both**: ESLint clean (frontend), ruff/black (backend)

### When in Doubt
Ask: "Which `.ai/` file addresses this?"

Don't invent rules. Don't bypass tests. Don't hide errors.
